import{_ as a,o as t,c as s,a5 as n}from"./chunks/framework.CsGesDJn.js";const h=JSON.parse('{"title":"Technical plan","description":"","frontmatter":{},"headers":[],"relativePath":"feature/content-task-workflow/workspace-task-real-data/plan.md","filePath":"feature/content-task-workflow/workspace-task-real-data/plan.md"}'),o={name:"feature/content-task-workflow/workspace-task-real-data/plan.md"};function i(r,e,l,d,c,p){return t(),s("div",null,[...e[0]||(e[0]=[n('<h1 id="technical-plan" tabindex="-1">Technical plan <a class="header-anchor" href="#technical-plan" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Technical plan&quot;">​</a></h1><h2 id="demo-isolation-correction-2026-10-16" tabindex="-1">Demo isolation correction (2026-10-16) <a class="header-anchor" href="#demo-isolation-correction-2026-10-16" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Demo isolation correction (2026-10-16)&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Remove only the TaskSampleSeeder dependency/call from WorkspaceTaskReader. Retain TaskSampleSeeder and its invocation from the opt-in MongoDataSeeder; do not run this seeder on Atlas. Extend reader regression tests to prove that empty/Untitled results cause only count/find reads. Run Campaign, Request, workflow, content-writing and publishing regression suites. Rehearse the five existing Request/Task migrations against an isolated clone of affected schema/data before Atlas APPLY, recheck fingerprints and keep existing Task documents unchanged. Business writers must be stopped; do not touch Post/Chat/Mail schemas in this change.</p><ol><li>Add typed Task list query/reader behind the existing TaskService/controller. Preserve old service signature for existing integrations; controller invokes a query-object overload. MongoTemplate filters/counts/pages TaskDocument with workspace criteria always applied. Validate types/status/search length/campaign ID, quote regex, stable sorting. Bulk-resolve only names/avatars via UserRepository (one lookup per page); extend list DTO with source metadata and description, not specialised editor content.</li><li>Web taskService uses the full versioned endpoint and typed envelope/page guards, forwards real filters, and never imports mockTaskService. useTasks handles errors, stale request cancellation and page reset. Remove local mutation-only hooks; preserve data on transient refresh only when scope matches, never display stale rows on error/scope change.</li><li>Expand Task type/status constants and filters. Display unknown priority as missing. Retain layout; add read-only actual Task summary dialog and current-page pagination on all views. Add <code>tasks.json</code> in vi/en and register in i18n/index.ts.</li><li>Keep Calendar layout but remove generated date/allDay/duration/venue/category assumptions; show deadlines only and disable editing/selecting. Kanban groups every actual status with no local drag mutations. Gantt retains rows/day-grid, uses true dueDate markers and date navigation, no fake bar spans or drag state.</li><li>Unit tests: reader query/access/DTO mapping, service error/empty/filter contracts, date/board mapping. Focused Maven/Vitest + type/build/lint and Playwright CLI isolated browser with mocked transport and actual UI. Do not read real tokens or mutate shared Atlas. No migration necessary: existing Campaign/Request stores already persist required fields.</li></ol><h2 id="local-handoff" tabindex="-1">Local handoff <a class="header-anchor" href="#local-handoff" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Local handoff&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li>Restart Business Service to load the new reader/controller query contract, then reload Web. Gateway is unchanged.</li><li>No PostgreSQL or Mongo migration, seed, init or backfill is required for this integration.</li><li>The endpoint retains Spring Page serialization (<code>number</code> is the current page). Web normalizes <code>number</code> to its local <code>page</code> field; both shapes have regression coverage.</li><li>Test using existing accounts and a Workspace whose Campaign deployment has succeeded. Planned work items alone do not appear until deployment creates their generic Tasks. Accepted Content Requests use the same list, retain campaignId/sourceRefId, and do not change the approved plan.</li><li>List, Kanban, Calendar and timeline use the current server-filtered page; navigate pagination to see more. Missing deadlines stay visible in List/Kanban, with an explanation in date views.</li><li>This release is read-only, as confirmed by the user. Persisted status/date dragging, assignment and specialised content editors remain separate work. No claim that all FR 3.6.4-3.6.8 are complete.</li><li>Existing mockTaskService source is retained for unrelated consumers/tests, but real Task list transport does not import or fall back to it. No changes to other members&#39; specialised modules, stashes, data, or automatic commit/push.</li></ul>',6)])])}const m=a(o,[["render",i]]);export{h as __pageData,m as default};
